@title Sensor provisioning
@subtitle Brightleaf Greenhouses field engineering, from the IoT platform team, dated 2026-10-14

## Provisioning sequence
diagram prov sequence title="Sensor provisioning"
prov: sensor "Sensor" device
prov: gw "Gateway" svc
prov: ps "Provisioning Service" svc
prov: ca "Certificate Authority" ext
prov: reg "Device Registry" db
prov: sensor -> gw : BLE pairing request with serial
prov: gw -> ps : claim device with one-time token
prov: ps -> reg : look up serial and token
prov: reg --> ps : record, status unclaimed
prov: ps -> ca : certificate signing request
prov: ca --> ps : signed certificate, valid 365 days
prov: ps -> reg : mark device active
prov: ps --> gw : certificate and MQTT endpoint
prov: gw -> sensor : install certificate
prov: sensor -> gw : first telemetry over TLS

## Limits and timeouts
table = item,value; One-time token validity,24 hours; Pairing window on the sensor,90 seconds; Signing key type,ECDSA P-256; Claim attempts before the token is locked,3; Certificate lifetime,365 days

## When provisioning fails
- **Token expired:** request a new token from the dashboard.
- **Pairing window closed:** press and hold the button for 5 seconds.
- **Token locked after 3 attempts:** contact IoT support at #iot-support.

!! Never photograph the one-time token QR code.
